# RG35XX RC1 integration specification — native media events to PlatformPlayer
# Task: RGJ-RC1-010E
# Status target: IMPLEMENTED contract only; not BUILD-PASS.

OWNERSHIP
- Java -> native audio commands remain on the dedicated RG35XX audio FD.
- Java stdout remains binary video IPC only; never write media events there.
- Native -> Java media completion reuses the already-existing libretro-core ->
  Libretro.java stdin control channel. Do not add a second reverse pipe/thread.
- RG35XXMediaRegistry owns player-id lookup and a bounded event queue.
- PlatformPlayer remains the MMAPI/vendor listener facade.

EXACT LIBRETRO SOURCE FINDING
- Upstream Libretro.java parses a 5-byte control header: one opcode followed by
  a big-endian 32-bit value named `code`.
- Existing cases include 13=run jar and 15=frame/update tick.
- Case 14 is unused in the inspected devel source and is reserved here for
  RG35XX native-media events.

CASE 14 WIRE FORMAT
Header:
  byte 0    = 14
  bytes 1-4 = big-endian payload length, MUST equal 13
Payload (13 bytes):
  byte 0    = event type (1 END_OF_MEDIA, 2 LOOPED)
  bytes 1-4 = big-endian player id
  bytes 5-12= big-endian unsigned media time in microseconds

Libretro.java case 14 must:
1. Require code == 13; otherwise discard/ignore safely.
2. Read exactly 13 payload bytes (loop until full or EOF); a single read() is
   not sufficient for pipe correctness.
3. Decode player id/media time without allocating helper objects.
4. Call RG35XXMediaRegistry.enqueueNativeEvent(playerId,eventType,timeUs).
5. Return immediately to the stdin parser; do NOT invoke MIDlet listeners from
   case 14 itself.

CASE 15 DRAIN
- The existing case 15 frame/update tick is the bounded Java-side cadence.
- After existing core-update/input-repeat work, call
  RG35XXMediaRegistry.drainNativeEvents().
- No Timer, executor, extra event thread or polling worker is introduced.
- Queue is a fixed 32-event primitive ring; overflow drops oldest stale event
  rather than blocking the Libretro IO parser.

PLATFORMPLAYER BINDING
For an RG35XXNativePlayer backend, PlatformPlayer binds one reusable
RG35XXMediaRegistry.EventListener:
- EVENT_END_OF_MEDIA:
    set facade state to Player.PREFETCHED, then call existing
    notifyListeners(PlayerListener.END_OF_MEDIA, mediaTimeUs).
- EVENT_LOOPED:
    keep playback semantic state appropriate to the native loop, then call
    existing notifyListeners(PlayerListener.LOOPED, mediaTimeUs).

Do not duplicate vendor dispatch. Existing PlatformPlayer.notifyListeners()
already translates events for MIDP, Siemens, Nokia, KDDI, DoJa and JBlend and
must remain the only facade notification fan-out.

NATIVE CALLBACK
- rg35xx_mixer / rg35xx_midi_backend completion must be converted by the
  consolidated libretro core into case-14 packets on the existing core->Java
  stdin pipe.
- Final completion must emit END_OF_MEDIA exactly once.
- Intermediate native loops should emit LOOPED so KDDI/DoJa/JBlend loop events
  are not lost. Current native modules do not yet expose a proven intermediate
  MIDI-loop callback; this remains an explicit RC1 gate and prevents declaring
  the full media facade STATIC-AUDIT-PASS.

LIFECYCLE
- RELEASE removes the registry entry/listener; late events for released IDs are
  ignored.
- RESET/game unload clears the event ring together with registry entries.
- No event may survive into the next JAR after RG35XXLifecycle reset.

ROLLBACK
- Remove case 14 + registry event binding together if the native reverse-event
  bridge is not consolidated. Never fall back to Java timers for END_OF_MEDIA.
